| Smart quotes and apostrophes regularised
|   set "forcers" to normal unambiguous chars
|   Note both input and output are DUSCI
| 1;1  2014-10-29/J E Sullivan
| 1;2  2015-11-10/jes: refine logic towards defaults with only conservative
|      exceptions (ex0001)
| 2;1  2016-06-14/15/jes: Complete revision - base decision on local context only
|      (no longer on whether or not there's an unclosed single quote) -- rather
|      on whether there are alphanumerics somewhere to left and/or immediately
|      to right
| 2;2  2016-06-16/jes: make
|      quıØ -> qu'
|      a rule also in state 2 (for lorsqu')(ex0009)
| 2;3  2017-05-05/jes: when the first ' in 'n' or 'N' is forced to apostrophe (in
|      state 1 only), treat the second as apostrophe also if ambiguous;
|      accommodate
|        D+b279 D%|178|121 D:≤y U+0149 Latin small letter n preceded by apostrophe
|      by converting to ordinary 'n sequence -- and also treat any following '
|      as apostrophe
| 2;4  2026-09-25/cln: added a rule to fix badly constructed [idle~lfs] codes.
| States:
|   1 no alphanumerics since last space or spacing formatting code
|   2 after alphanumerics since last space or spacing code
|   3 after prefix enroute to state 1
|   4 after prefix enroute to state 2
|   5 in format/translation code passing through to |031 or space (preserving state)
| extra rule added by cln to fix a problem with badly constructed [idle~lfs] codes.
|028idle |~3lfs|031~|028idle|~lfs|031~
